# The pack payload is a BUILD artifact (P2-5): `python tools/build_asset_packs.py build-local`
# copies the mt6989 encoder and writes the pair's metadata.json here from the private artefact
# store, every byte checked against the census's own literals on the way in and re-hashed out of
# the directory afterwards. NeuroPilot-compiled bytecode must never enter a repo with a public
# remote, and the root .gitignore's blob walls (*.so, *.dlc, *.context) do not cover .bin — so
# this pattern IS the wall.
#
# The wall is written as "everything in the payload directory EXCEPT the anchor" — the preview
# packs' untargeted shape — rather than as the one file name: anything else placed here would be
# committable by default, and everything in this directory rides into the AAB.
#
# The .gitkeep is TRACKED and is the one file here that must stay visible to git: it is what
# proves the payload directory exists in a clean clone, and NpuPackLayoutTest reads the directory
# from the repo. The negation can only re-include a DIRECT child, which is why the wall stops at
# the payload directory's contents instead of walling src/main/assets/ wholesale.
src/main/assets/npu_turbo_mt6989_enc/*
!src/main/assets/npu_turbo_mt6989_enc/.gitkeep
